Winnow Solutions, a London-based technology company, develops AI-powered food waste tracking systems for commercial kitchens. Their Winnow Vision system uses a camera positioned above waste bins combined with machine learning to automatically identify, weigh, and log discarded food items. The system generates detailed analytics dashboards showing exactly what is being wasted, when, and in what quantities. Hotels, restaurants, and caterers using Winnow have achieved average food waste reductions of 50%, translating to typical annual savings of £30,000-£100,000 per site. IKEA deployed Winnow across 36 stores in 22 countries, cutting food waste by 54% within 12 months. The system works through behaviour steering: making waste visible to kitchen staff in real time creates an immediate feedback loop that changes preparation habits. Winnow demonstrates how resource monitoring technology can fundamentally alter operational behaviour without imposing restrictions, instead empowering informed decision-making through data visibility.